From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@docker01.fra.askei.net>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:36:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat(moe_wna16): 2-bit experts, expert streaming,
 N-contiguous GEMV

Port the accepted INT2/streaming changes onto main b02e16a895.

- kernel: 2-bit unpack in fused_moe_kernel_gptq_awq and the word-load int2
  branch (fused_moe_kernel_gptq_awq_word) for the tiled prefill kernel, with
  int2_w2a16 config-dtype naming so an int4 config is never picked up.
- runner: use_int2_w2a16 plumbing and N-contiguous [E, K/16, N] int32 grid
  handling; the fused-swiglu interleaved guard now also rejects int2.
- loader: 2-bit moe_wna16 loader (asymmetric qzeros raise), N-contiguous
  re-layout in process_weights_after_loading, expert placement collection and
  the batch-1 GEMV dispatch (M <= 16) through int64 address tables.
- expert_stream.py: MoE-aware ExpertStreamer that moves only the routed
  experts across PCIe; also carries the accepted PP prefetch/ gather-DMA
  helpers (their model-side wiring follows with the PP commit).
- expert_gemv.py: in-place int2 GEMV and to_word_ncontig.

The measurement-only prefill route dump hook is not ported. Placement and
elastic residency modules, lazy KV, quantized QSA, PP and RC/RB follow.
